<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tarusbawa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tarusbawa is remembered in later Sundanese tradition as the founder of the Sunda Kingdom of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>. According to texts such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carita-parahyangan">Carita Parahyangan</a> tradition, in 669 he took the western part of the former Tarumanagara lands, while the eastern part beyond the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/citarum-river">Citarum River</a> became the Galuh Kingdom. No contemporary inscription confirms these traditional dates.</p></div>
